.TH "hey" "1" "2026-06-30" "hey(1)" "Documentation Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
hey - local-first note retrieval tool for programmers
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
hey [keywords.\&.\&.\&]
.br
hey .\& [keywords.\&.\&.\&]
.br
hey [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBhey\fR is a local-first note retrieval tool designed for storing and
retrieving programmer notes.\&
.PP
Notes are stored as plain files on the local machine.\& Searches are
performed against note titles, which are treated as collections of
retrieval keywords.\&
.PP
Unlike full-text note search systems, \fBhey\fR currently searches note
titles only.\& Users are encouraged to choose descriptive titles that
reflect the contents of each note.\&
.PP
Example note titles:
.br
	rust ownership
.br
	rust traits
.br
	asm directives
.br
	linux namespaces
.PP
Search results are ranked according to the number of matching keywords.\&
.PP
The project prioritizes:
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
Local-first storage
.IP \(bu 4
Human-readable files
.IP \(bu 4
Deterministic behavior
.IP \(bu 4
Simplicity
.IP \(bu 4
Unix-inspired workflows
.PD
.PP
.RE
The project intentionally avoids:
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
Cloud services
.IP \(bu 4
AI-powered retrieval
.IP \(bu 4
Remote synchronization
.PD
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.SS -h, --help
.PP
Display a concise help message and exit.\&
.PP
.SS --help-verbose
.PP
Display detailed documentation and exit.\&
.PP
.SS -v, --version
.PP
Display version information and exit.\&
.PP
.SS ., --new [keywords...]
.PP
Create a new note using the supplied keywords as its title.\&
.PP
Example:
.br
	hey .\& rust ownership
.PP
.SH SEARCH
.PP
Any argument sequence not interpreted as an option is treated as a
search query.\&
.PP
Example:
.br
	hey rust ownership
.PP
Searches are currently performed against note titles only.\&
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
.SS HEY_EDITOR
.PP
Editor command used by \fBhey\fR.\&
.PP
If set, this variable takes precedence over all other editor
configuration.\&
.PP
.SS VISUAL
.PP
Used when `HEY_EDITOR` is not set.\&
.PP
.SS EDITOR
.PP
Used when neither `HEY_EDITOR` nor `VISUAL` are set.\&
.PP
.SH EDITOR SELECTION
.PP
Editors are selected using the following precedence order:
.br
	1.\& HEY_EDITOR
.br
	2.\& VISUAL
.br
	3.\& EDITOR
.br
	4.\& Platform default
.PP
Platform defaults:
.br
	Unix-like systems : vi
.br
	Windows           : notepad
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
hey stores its data in an operating-system appropriate application data
directory.\&
.PP
.SS Typical locations:
.PP
- \fBLinux\fR
.br
	\(ti/.\&local/share/hey
.br
- \fBWindows\fR
.br
	%LOCALAPPDATA%hey
.br
- \fBmacOS\fR
.br
	\(ti/Library/Application Support/hey
.PP
Notes are stored within the application'\&s managed notes directory.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
- Create a note:
.br
	hey .\& rust ownership
.br
- Search for notes:
.br
	hey rust ownership
.br
- Display help:
.br
	hey --help
.br
- Display detailed help:
.br
	hey --help-verbose
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
.SS 0
.PP
Successful execution.\&
.PP
.SS Non-zero
.PP
An error occurred.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
vi(1), vim(1), nvim(1)
